From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm_hwcomposer: report extra cursor planes once per pipeline

GetUsablePlanes() runs several times for every frame. When the DRM
device lists more than one cursor plane for a CRTC, it logs
"Encountered multiple cursor planes" on every call. The SC8280XP DPU
registers both of its cursor-capable pipes as cursor planes usable on
every CRTC, so the internal display logs about 200 of these lines per
second while the screen updates. The message itself is harmless, but
it crowds everything else out of the log buffer and keeps being
mistaken for the cause of unrelated hangs.

Log it once per pipeline, and say that later cursor planes are skipped
too. The choice of cursor plane is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.cpp | 11 +++++++----
 drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.h   |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.cpp b/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.cpp
index 1c5b7e1..b91e564 100644
--- a/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.cpp
@@ -155,10 +155,13 @@ auto DrmDisplayPipeline::GetUsablePlanes() const -> UsablePlanes {
         }
       } else if (plane->GetType() == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR) {
         if (cursor) {
-          ALOGW(
-              "Encountered multiple cursor planes for CRTC %d. Ignoring "
-              "plane %d",
-              crtc->Get()->GetId(), plane->GetId());
+          if (!extra_cursor_plane_reported.exchange(true)) {
+            ALOGW(
+                "Encountered multiple cursor planes for CRTC %d. Ignoring "
+                "plane %d and any further cursor planes (logged once per "
+                "pipeline)",
+                crtc->Get()->GetId(), plane->GetId());
+          }
         } else {
           cursor = plane->BindPipeline(this, true);
         }
diff --git a/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.h b/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.h
index 00da5d6..cf2b893 100644
--- a/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.h
+++ b/drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.h
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <atomic>
 #include <memory>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -109,6 +110,10 @@ struct DrmDisplayPipeline {
 
   std::unique_ptr<DrmAtomicCommitSink> atomic_commit_sink;
   std::unique_ptr<CompositionPlanner> planner;
+
+  /* GetUsablePlanes() runs for every frame, so report extra cursor planes
+   * only once per pipeline. */
+  mutable std::atomic_bool extra_cursor_plane_reported{false};
 };
 
 }  // namespace android::drm_hwcomposer
